# Ampersand vs plus

In user-facing copy, nav labels, headings, and site writing, prefer **+** over **&**.

| Prefer | Avoid (site voice) |
|--------|--------------------|
| Residencies + Workshops | Residencies & Workshops |
| Railway + steamships | Railway & steamships |
| Theory + Practice | Theory & Practice |

## Keep `&` when it is not our voice

Leave ampersands that belong to **citations, bibliographic publishers, or legal/official names** we are quoting accurately:

- Publisher names in citations (`McClelland & Stewart`)
- Cited titles that use `&` (`Heritage: Newfoundland & Labrador`, book titles)
- Institution legal names (`Leonard & Bina Ellen Art Gallery`)

Do not rewrite those to `+`.

## Also

- Prefer `+` in Cursor rules and docs for this repo when joining two nouns (same house style)
- Do not change `&` in URLs, HTML entities, or code (`&&`, query strings)
